// ADR-009 E2 #18 slice 3 — a CLOSURE-BEARING replace-body EDIT installs and runs
// NATIVELY in both tiers under `--mode jit`, printing 42 (the POST-edit
// replacement, not the pre-edit 7). The replacement carries an explicit
// `move`-capture closure — the C0911 shape slice-3 materializes pre-analysis so
// the analyzer publishes its structural fact (the LSP flip); pass-2 performs the
// authoritative body swap. The `move base` closure runs NATIVE post-C1 #12
// (1f0127a3): C1's slice-4 zero-fallback matrix (9/9) proved declared-capture
// closures JIT natively, and this is exactly that class — so JIT == VM with zero
// [jit-fallback]. No async, trait/impl, or top-level comptime block (an
// annotation `comptime post` handler is not a top-level comptime block), so the
// fixture is not silently excluded from native JIT — the zero-fallback is real.
annotation edit_answer() on function {
  comptime post(target, ctx) {
    replace body {
      let base = 40
      let worker = |; move base| base + 2
      return worker()
    }
  }
}

@edit_answer()
fn answer() -> int { 7 }

print(answer())
